 of v2.3.1 failure, and note that v2.2.9 predates the v2.3.0 CVE fix \u2014 assess whether a patched forward-fix is needed.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-2.2.9"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Done. Summary:\n\n**Findings**\n- checkout-api was on v2.3.1 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), unhealthy with an 18% error rate.\n- Release history: v2.2.9 (healthy) \u2192 v2.3.0 (healthy) \u2192 v2.3.1 (unhealthy). v2.3.1-rc was staging-only and also unhealthy.\n\n**Actions**\n1. Attempted rollback to **v2.3.0** (most recent healthy production release) \u2014 **rejected**: v2.3.0 is quarantined due to CVE-2026-4417.\n2. Rolled back to **v2.2.9**, the next most recent release that was healthy in production \u2014 succeeded in all three regions.\n3. Opened **INC-0001 (SEV2)** for checkout-api; the on-call engineer has been paged. The incident describes the failure, the quarantine block on v2.3.0, and the rollback to v2.2.9.\n\n**One thing to flag:** v2.2.9 predates whatever v2.3.0 may have changed relative to CVE-2026-4417, so I noted in the incident that the team should assess whether a patched forward-fix is needed rather than staying on v2.2.9 long-term. I did not deploy any version that hasn't been healthy in production, so no change-manager approval was required.", "type": "text"}]}]}